								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=49"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.mikemill.org" title="My Web Page" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12948#msg12948"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12948#msg12948">Re: Relief for us smelly bards.  LOL</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> December 06, 2004, 10:39:36 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Oh thank god I&#039;m no longer playing.&nbsp; It seems that SoE is despreate to hold on to the few (compared to what they had before) players they have left.
