								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12953#msg12953">Re: Relief for us smelly bards.  LOL</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #4 on:</b> December 06, 2004, 02:30:37 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							There is a reson why when you start the character that it is clasified as a Hard character.&nbsp; I know I tryed to play a bard and it was difficult for me to get the timing down on twisting songs.&nbsp; My hats off to the bards that make this happen flawlessly.&nbsp; My only problem is with like someone stated before that it will make it to easy to play a bard.&nbsp; I think there are so many other problems that that should be addressing other than making ANOTHER character super easy to play.&nbsp; &nbsp;I mean realy why don&#039;t they just send a person over to your house and have them tell you how to play the character LOL .......Well you know what I mean.&nbsp; I thought leveling up to 5 outside the game in the tutorial was stupid and then I find out they scribe your first level spells.&nbsp; Are we not suposed to figure this all out as we play the game more .&nbsp; My personal view is that Sony is making this way to easy for people ,make them find out how to scribe spells....get backpacks.....LEVEL for gosh sakes LOL but Im rambling so sorry :D<br /><br />Eshebala
						</td>
