	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12963"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=371" title="View the profile of Shakro">Shakro</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 32<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/coolbear.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								<a href="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/about_me/1,,,00.html?Uin=24026767" target="_blank"><img src="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/online?icq=24026767&amp;img=5" alt="24026767" width="18" height="18" border="0" /></a>
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=371"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12963#msg12963"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12963#msg12963">Re: Relief for us smelly bards.  LOL</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #10 on:</b> December 06, 2004, 07:46:08 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I&#039;m all in favor of keeping the game hard, keeping things so that good players stand out and you have an opportunity to demonstrate skill.&nbsp; But twisting songs just turns EQ into a twitch game, not a skill one.&nbsp; Would it show skill if you had to hit a button to attack instead of pressing &quot;A&quot;?&nbsp; Melody eliminates a major annoyance in playing bards and&nbsp; reduces the very real risk of carpal tunnel syndrome.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Shakro Shakdaddy<br />68 Hekoyah of Bertoxxulous<br />Brew Masters
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12964"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=361" title="View the profile of Toastie">Toastie</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 43<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=361"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12964#msg12964"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12964#msg12964">Re: Relief for us smelly bards.  LOL</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #11 on:</b> December 06, 2004, 09:13:40 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							you make it sound like twisting is the hardest thing ever, and that its more of a burdon then anything else to playing a bard effectively. <br /> <br />when to be completely honest, i cant comprehend how anyone could play a bard effectively while using this auto-twisting program... you cant switch the songs your twisting on a whim without even really thinking about it.&nbsp; so debuffing / mezing etc all happen slower etc.&nbsp; and i dont have any faith that this will help bards play better and smarter.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12965"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=371" title="View the profile of Shakro">Shakro</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 32<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/coolbear.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								<a href="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/about_me/1,,,00.html?Uin=24026767" target="_blank"><img src="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/online?icq=24026767&amp;img=5" alt="24026767" width="18" height="18" border="0" /></a>
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=371"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12965#msg12965"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12965#msg12965">Re: Relief for us smelly bards.  LOL</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #12 on:</b> December 06, 2004, 09:27:06 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							They&#039;re not getting rid of the option to play songs the way you normally do, just giving bards some versatility.&nbsp; And to be honest, this isn&#039;t anything new - bards have been using macros and programmable gamepads to auto-twist for some time now.&nbsp; Probably many in groups you were in already, and you didn&#039;t even realize it.&nbsp; <br /><br />This probably won&#039;t make people who play bards better players.&nbsp; But it will make bards more user-friendly and probably will encourage more people to play the class.&nbsp; There&#039;s a reason that what is undoubtably the most versatile class in the game, great in groups, great in raids, great solo, is probably the least-played class besides zerkers.&nbsp; 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Shakro Shakdaddy<br />68 Hekoyah of Bertoxxulous<br />Brew Masters
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12970"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=117" title="View the profile of Memadil">Memadil</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 48<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I&#039;m a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=117"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12970#msg12970"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12970#msg12970">Re: Relief for us smelly bards.  LOL</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #13 on:</b> December 07, 2004, 12:13:20 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							O yeah Toastie the game is very, very different from the time I started playing until now.&nbsp; I guess SoE is slowly realizing...how do i put this, to listen and watch the people that play the game? Look at how they have changed the default UI, being able to alt+tab out of the game without the use of EQW, etc.&nbsp; Most bards do use macros and other sorta things to autotwist, SoE is just now coming out with their own &quot;macro&quot;.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=510588" target="_blank">Memadil Rahl</a><br />65 Druid
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12979"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=917" title="View the profile of EshetheShammy">EshetheShammy</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Officer<br />
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 47<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/boobies.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I know you wanna look<br />
								<br />
								
								
								<a href="http://edit.yahoo.com/config/send_webmesg?.target=Messhaller"><img src="http://opi.yahoo.com/online?u=Messhaller&amp;m=g&amp;t=0" alt="Messhaller" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="aim:goim?screenname=Messhaller&amp;message=Hi.+Are+you+there?"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/aim.gif" alt="Messhaller" border="0" /></a><br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=917"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:Messhaller@aol.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12979#msg12979"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1308.msg12979#msg12979">Re: Relief for us smelly bards.  LOL</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #14 on:</b> December 07, 2004, 02:47:35 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Im not saying autotwist is a bad thing I just think the more that they add &quot;convinences&quot; (sp)&nbsp; that people will expect more....Such as when I mentioned the spells being scribed for you ect.&nbsp; I have been playing for 3 years myself and have seen many changes some are good some are bad in my mind.... LOL like the tradeskill window OMG can you make it any easier remember when you had to make Halas 10lb pies by hand!&nbsp; this is like haveing them frozen and all you have to do is heat it up LOL.....Oh well what are ya going to do ehh???&nbsp; <br /><br /><br />Love <br />Eshebala
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />66 Shaman<br />Drunken Fishermen<br />RN
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
